==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-}}
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-||to command, to persuade, to trust}}.
Cognate to {{cog|la|fīdō||I trust}} and {{cog|gem-pro|*bīdaną}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|fidēs}}

====Noun====
{{la-noun|fidēs<5>}}

# [[faith]], [[belief]] {{gloss|belief without empirical evidence, direct experience, or observation}}
# [[reliance]] {{gloss|act of relying on or trusting}}
#: {{syn|la|fīdūcia}}
# [[confidence]], [[trust]] {{gloss|confidence in or reliance on some person or quality}}
# [[credit]] {{gloss|acceptance of the truth of something said or done}}
# [[loyalty]], [[fidelity]], faith {{gloss|state of demonstrating undivided and constant support for someone or something}}
# [[good faith]] {{gloss|good, honest intentions}}
# [[honesty]] {{gloss|act, quality, or condition of being honest}}
# [[guarantee]], [[promise]] {{gloss|an assurance of something to be done}}
#: {{syn|la|prōmissum|pollicitum|prōmissiō|crēdentia}}
# [[help]], [[assistance]]
#: {{syn|la|adiūtus|adiumentum|auxilium|subsidium|ops|praesidium}}
#* {{Q|la|Titus Livius|Ab Urbe Condita|I|7|quote='''Fidem''' pastorum nequiquam invocans|t=vainly appealing for '''help''' to the shepherds}}

